[Music]  well i'm alex kirford  i'm the founder of the corporate chess  league financial advisor and captain  of team edward jones so the whole  concept  of the corporate chess league was an  opportunity to bring together  companies individuals in a way that  could be competitive  it could be fun and be able to  better engage with some of your  colleagues and so prior to  the pandemic and covet 19 we were able  to gather here  in the chess club meet face to face and  have games on a quarterly basis  it was a lot of fun had a high level of  engagement  and people beginning to be attracted to  that edward jones has been thrilled  to be to help found but also to  participate in the corporate chess  league  and this year actually it's been a  little bit of a change now that we've  gone virtual  our audience has grown we absolutely  love the corporate chess league i can  tell you  my teammates and i we feel like we're  truly a team and we practice  we have regular practices and we take it  seriously it  has really expanded and the engagement  to want to play  even more has happened during this time  so we took  quarterly meetings to now being able to  put on the corporate chess league  once a month here at edward jones we  actually have  people all over north america about 50  000 close to  associates all over north america i have  a really good friend in the phoenix area  who's passionate about chess  it's hard for him to fly out just to  play into a tournament so now that it's  been virtual  he's been participating on the team as  well so in order to capture the essence  of the purpose of the corporate chess  league  we've been able to provide an experience  where  prior to the competition of chess  actually begins  people are able to come into our google  hangouts page  and be able to see and interact with  each other  in a virtual way and then partnering  with chess.com we're able to provide  the the actual uh tournament and and how  the competition begins  and the corporate chess league allows us  as a team a to bond  and we're doing really well as a team  i'm happy to say and b it allows us to  kind of  you know rib each other a little bit and  and it is a little friendly banter which  we love  and all during that time the st louis  chess club is hosting  a youtube channel that has commentary  from  guest speakers grand masters  international masters  commentating on how the games are  actually going that makes for  a lot of fun for people to be able to  see  how their friends how their colleagues  are doing  during a game by having a professional  be able to speak about  the position and and have fun that way  too  i think during this time it is hard  for to have motivation sometimes we can  get  down on things having an outlet where  competition  can still be involved in your life  having an  outlet where you can still have  networking with your colleagues  has really been a key part of the  success  of the corporate chess league it has  been really fun to be able to not only  get to know the people in my  own firm better and share that that  similar passion  but also get to know people from several  different  firms here in in the st louis area  we've continued to have interest in the  corporate chess league both here in the  st  louis area and beyond we're looking  forward to a great season  in 2021 if you or your company  is interested in being a part of the  corporate chess league  you can go to www.stlouischessclub.org  and get more information we'd love to  have you be a part of the competition  you

